      "writtenOn": "2026-04-21T14:08:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right. This rule is not necessary in all these cases:\n\n* plugins provide own rule for test dependencies, and we shouldn\u0027t break them\n* there is no external test dependencies\n* plugin maintainers don\u0027t use eclipse\n\nTo address all issues, should we rather have special parameter for this rule, e.g. `expose_test_deps_for_plugin \u003d \"\"`?\n\nAnd then do something if it was actually provided, like this:\n\n```python\n if expose_test_deps_for_plugin:\n   java_library(\n       name \u003d expose_test_deps_for_plugin + \"__plugin_test_deps\",\n       [...]\n```",
      "parentUuid": "1f0be3e4_0016703c",
      "revId": "869a1334ea9df16f8e5d4204265c561d6c8240f9",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
